      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Statutory Framework: Greek Law 4758/2020 &amp; Article 5C Legal Architecture
      </h2>
      <p>
        In December 2020, the Hellenic Parliament enacted <strong>Law 4758/2020</strong>, introducing <strong>Article 5C</strong> into the Greek Income Tax Code (Law 4172/2013). This legislation was conceived as a structural economic instrument to counteract severe domestic brain drain and position Greece as a premier Mediterranean hub for high-skilled digital professionals, software engineers, and global remote founders.
      </p>
      <p>
        The immigration pathway is codified under <strong>Law 4825/2021 (Article 11)</strong>, which formally created the Greek Digital Nomad Visa (DNV). Unlike golden visa programs that demand non-productive real estate capital or passive wealth investments, the Greek digital nomad framework specifically targets active economic value creation. It provides a legal mechanism for third-country nationals (citizens outside the European Union, European Economic Area, and Switzerland) to reside legally in Greece while executing contracts exclusively for employers or clients incorporated abroad.
      </p>
      <p>
        The fiscal mechanism under Article 5C is simple yet potent: <strong>50% of your total gross employment or freelance income generated while resident in Greece is entirely exempt from income tax</strong>. The remaining 50% of income is subjected to standard progressive tax brackets, effectively halving the tax burden across every bracket tier for seven consecutive calendar years.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
