        <li><strong>€30,001 to €40,000</strong>: 36% marginal tax rate</li>
        <li><strong>€40,001 and above</strong>: 44% marginal tax rate</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Under Article 5C, your gross earnings are halved prior to applying the progressive rate table. Furthermore, recent tax reforms have permanently repealed the Special Solidarity Contribution (Eisfora Allilegiis) for private sector employment and business income, guaranteeing that your sole income tax liability matches the reduced bracket schedule.
      </p>

